(footprint "Nordic_nRF9151_LGA-113_12.1x11.1mm_P0.5mm"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "uwb_rescue_locator_lib_builder")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Nordic nRF9151 SiP, 113-pad LGA, body 12.1 x 11.1 mm (11.1 along X, 12.1 along Y here), 0.5 mm pitch, 1.3 mm max height. Pad geometry is Nordic's own: extracted from the footprint LGA50P1210X1110X130-113N placed as M1 in Nordic's nRF9151 DK (PCA10171 v1.0.1) Altium PcbDoc 400797.PcbDoc, from 'nRF9151 Development Kit - Hardware files 1_0_0.zip' on nordicsemi.com (Products > Development hardware > nRF9151-DK > Download). All 113 pad centres and sizes were independently confirmed against flashes in the same package's top-copper Gerber 400797.GTL. Pad numbers 1-113 are the PcbDoc pad designators and agree with the bay_station:nRF9151 symbol (GND on corners 1/20/41/60 and centre pads 105-113, RSVD on 81-104). Pin 1 is bottom-left, numbering counter-clockwise viewed from the top. Edge pads 0.3 x 0.45 mm, corner pads 0.7 x 0.7 mm (pin 1 is 0.45 x 0.7 in the source), inner RSVD pads 0.3 x 0.3 mm, ground pads 1.6 x 1.6 mm and 1.95 x 1.6 mm. Mask and paste apertures are NOT taken from the DK (they are Altium rules, not stored on the pads): KiCad board defaults apply, and the large ground pads need reduced paste apertures decided with the fab stencil. Not cross-checked against the nRF9151 PS mechanical-specification land-pattern figure (Nordic PDF not obtainable).")
	(tags "Nordic nRF9151 LGA-113 SiP LTE-M")
